# Local dev working folder + cross-project coordination channel — never committed.
# See dev-docs/README.md and inbox/README.md for the canonical layouts, and the
# dev-docs-cleanup / read-inbox skills for the auto-purged time-boxed tiers within.
#
# ONE exception: `bench/scripts/` IS tracked. Those harnesses are hand-authored
# source that exists in exactly one copy, in a tier the README says is never
# purged — so a stray `rm -rf` there loses work no backup, review or CI ever
# saw. `bench/out/` and `bench/results/` stay local. Everything a harness
# *produces* is re-excluded below, because on 2026-07-29 that tier held 857 MB
# of cargo `target/` output and 177 MB of audio next to ~200 KB of actual code.
# (`/dir/*` + `!/dir/sub/` so a subdir can be re-included.)
/dev-docs/*
!/dev-docs/bench/
/dev-docs/bench/*
!/dev-docs/bench/scripts/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/target/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/__pycache__/
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/node_modules/
# Audio: 20 s excerpts of commercial recordings (blind-review packets) and
# synthesized perception-gate controls. Local-only by policy — see
# bench/scripts/aggression-blind-review/INDEX.md.
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.wav
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.flac
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/**/*.mp3
# The SEALED held-out evaluation labels. Publishing them would defeat the seal
# (INDEX.md: "contents withheld, hash only"); they need an offsite *private*
# home, not this public repo.
/dev-docs/bench/scripts/aggression-blind-review/locked_labels.json
/inbox/

# Coverage / profiling
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
htmlcov/
flamegraph.svg
perf.data
